{title: I Am Coming to the Cross}
{artist: William McDonald / William G. Fischer}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 103}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 278)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I am coming to the cross;
[G]I am poor and weak and [D]blind;
[G]I am counting all but dross;
[C]I shall [G]full salvation find.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]I am trusting, Lord, in Thee.
[G]Blessèd Lamb of Calva[D]ry;
[G]Humbly at Thy cross I bow.
[C]Save me, [G]Jesus, save me now.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Long my heart has sighed for Thee;
[G]Long has evil reigned with[D]in;
[G]Jesus sweetly speaks to me:
[C]I will [G]cleanse you from all sin.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Here I give my all to Thee:
[G]Friends and time and earthly [D]store;
[G]Soul and body Thine to be,
[C]Wholly [G]Thine forevermore.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]In the promises I trust;
[G]Now I feel the blood ap[D]plied;
[G]I am prostrate in the dust;
[C]I with [G]Christ am crucified.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Jesus comes! He fills my soul!
[G]Perfected in Him I [D]am;
[G]I am every whit made whole:
[C]Glory, [G]glory to the Lamb!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
